e precise understanding of the physiology. You can say, "My grandma was right that babies handle the fluid just fine, and I now also know that's because the cord gives them time and they're holding their breath until they hit air." That's not a betrayal; that's growth. It's adding a layer, not tearing down the foundation. Your trust doesn't have to collapse. It can deepen. You're not rejecting your people; you're expanding what they gave you. And that's something to be proud of, not afraid of.
